<title>CANADA: CMHC sets C$200 million 5.5 pct bond due 2002.</title>
<headline>CMHC sets C$200 million 5.5 pct bond due 2002.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federally chartered Canadian Mortgage and Housing Corp set C$200 million of 5.5 percent bonds due September 3, 2002 in financial markets, lead manager RBC Dominion Securities Inc said.</p>
<p>The issue was priced at 100.315 with a yield of 5.427 percent, six basis points above the Government of Canada 5.5 percent bond due 2002.  </p>
<p>The non-callable debentures will be dated and delivered on July 30, 1997. The new issue is a reopening of a previous issue, the size of which now totals C$600 million.</p>
<p>((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com))</p>
